### Key design points across all three

| Concern | TypeScript | Python | Go |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Streaming source** | `fs.createReadStream` + `for await` loop | `open()` iterated line-by-line (`for line in f`) | `bufio.Scanner` over file handle (goroutine) |
| **Memory footprint** | Only one chunk at a time; each yielded item is held by the caller | One line parsed into memory, then discarded before next iteration | Each record unmarshaled and sent on channel; buffer 1024 items max |
| **Error handling** | `try/catch` per line, logs failure | `except json.JSONDecodeError`, prints & skips | `fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr)`, continues scanning |

All three assume the file is **NDJSON** (one JSON object per line). If your "large array" is a single big JSON array on disk, you'd need an external streaming parser or convert it to NDJSON first.
